[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3195951408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109724#issuecomment-3195951408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109724","id":3195951408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-flkw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T09:48:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T09:48:24Z","body":"While this does obviously emit the application focus events when you focus/unfocus the editor window, it still doesn't behave quite the same as with Windows and X11, where these events (along with `NOTIFICATION_WM_WINDOW_FOCUS_[IN|OUT]`) are emitted when the focus changes to/from the game viewport/workspace, just within the editor itself.\r\n\r\nIs that feasible/desirable to replicate with \"real\" embedding, like on macOS?\r\n\r\nPerhaps it's more of a philosophical question of whether the game is still considered a separate application/window even when embedded.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3195951408/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"